From c32b478b1b7c5c927ee9995f38b03f966fff535d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 00:55:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Surface the exact matched substrings when a Purchase
 Navigator report is rejected as contaminated

A live production test just failed with the generic message "Model output
contained malformed/leaked formatting artifacts" on both retry attempts,
meaning a real customer could hit this exact failure. The regex-based
contamination check (reportLooksContaminated) only reported that it fired,
not what it matched, making it impossible to tell from the stored error
whether this is a genuine leak (e.g. citation markup from web_search) or a
false positive (e.g. ordinary text like "<something> or <something else>"
that happens to look tag-shaped to the regex).

This change is diagnostic-only: it makes reportLooksContaminated collect
the matched substrings and includes up to 5 of them in the stored error
message on the navigator_submissions row, so the actual cause can be seen
without re-running anything. No behavior change to the success path, the
retry logic, or what the customer sees (navigator-status.html's generic
failure copy is unaffected either way).
